      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Given:\n- Number of students who took the test initially: \\(30\\)\n- Mean score of the first group (30 students): \\(72\\%\\)\n- Number of students who took the test next day: \\(6\\)\n- Mean score of the second group (6 students): \\(78\\%\\)\n\nWe need to find the new class mean after both groups have taken the test.\n\nFirst, calculate the total score for the first group:\n\\[\n\\text{Total score for the first group} = 30 \\times 72\\%\n\\]\n\\[\n= 30 \\times 0.72\n\\]\n\\[\n= 21.6\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate the total score for the second group:\n\\[\n\\text{Total score for the second group} = 6 \\times 78\\%\n\\]\n\\[\n= 6 \\times 0.78\n\\]\n\\[\n= 4.68\n\\]\n\nNow, find the overall total score for the entire class by adding the scores from both groups:\n\\[\n\\text{Total score for the entire class} = 21.6 + 4.68\n\\]\n\\[\n= 26.28\n\\]\n\nThe total number of students in the class is:\n\\[\n30 + 6 = 36\n\\]\n\nTo find the new class mean, divide the total score by the total number of students:\n\\[\n\\text{New class mean} = \\frac{26.28}{36}\n\\]\n\\[\n= 0.73\n\\]\n\nConvert the decimal to a percentage:\n\\[\n0.73 \\times 100\\% = 73\\%\n\\]\n\nThus, the new class mean is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{73\\%}\n\\]",
